WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.910
Private retrieval-augmented generation, often called private RAG,

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:06.950
can help AI systems answer from approved internal material.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:09.070
It can also create new responsibilities.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:13.730
Source documents must be ingested, chunked, embedded, indexed, retrieved, cited, updated,

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.200
expired, and permissioned.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.615
Treating RAG as only a vector database misses the governance work that makes the knowledge

00:00:19.615 --> 00:00:20.000
trustworthy.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.520
Knowledge control starts with source ownership and provenance.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.280
Teams should know where a document came from, who owns it, when it was ingested,

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.560
what version it represents, and whether it is current.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.080
Metadata matters because the AI system may retrieve fragments without the original context

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.980
that humans normally use to judge authority,

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.320
audience, and freshness.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.130
Permissions must survive retrieval.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:42.045
A user should not receive content through an AI answer that they could not access through

00:00:42.045 --> 00:00:42.940
the source system.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:46.515
Tenant boundaries, document-level permissions, collection-level permissions,

00:00:46.515 --> 00:00:48.080
and query-time enforcement all matter.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.650
It is not enough to protect the storage location if retrieval ignores the access rules.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.290
RAG quality also depends on lifecycle discipline.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.130
Old guidance can be retrieved as current.

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:58.880
Chunks can lose important qualifiers.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.100
Conflicting sources can appear side by side.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.670
Sensitive documents can enter the wrong collection.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:07.160
A sovereign AI program needs reviewable ingestion, retrieval testing,

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.648
source citations where appropriate, expiration rules, and update workflows.

00:01:10.648 --> 00:01:12.620
Retrieved text is context and evidence;

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:17.520
it should not be treated as unlimited authority over policy, law, or operational judgment.
